# Arc Foundry — Controls

This file fixes how a player operates the game: how simulation time advances, what the
pointer does, the actions the keyboard fires, and what each control on the status bar and
the build panel commits. Where those controls sit is in `specs/hud.md`, and what each
action produces is in `specs/scrap-press.md`.

## Simulation time

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
The frame loop is part of the runtime layer you write, and it hands each update the real
elapsed seconds of the frame.
{{else}}
The frame loop belongs to the {{engine.name}} engine, which hands each update the real
elapsed seconds of the frame.
{{/if}}

The game keeps a simulation clock, in seconds, and every duration and every rate this
specification states is measured against it.

| Situation | The clock advances by |
| --- | --- |
| A build phase, a wave, or the finale, not paused | `dt * speed`, where `speed` is the current speed multiplier |
| Paused in place, or the pause menu open | Nothing |
| Any screen other than `playing` | Nothing |

Every rate is per second and integrated against that advance, so an interval of
simulation time reaches the same state however it was divided into frames. The speed
multiplier changes how fast the game plays and never changes the outcome.

## The pointer

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
This game stands on no engine, so the pointer belongs to the runtime layer you write.
What the game reads from that layer is a pointer position in the game's logical units on
the `STAGE_W x STAGE_H` (`1280 x 720`) stage, a press edge, and a release edge. How the
layer produces them is yours to decide.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
The pointer belongs to the engine, which documents it in the `engine/` directory at the
root of this repository. What the game reads from it is a pointer position in the game's
logical units on the `STAGE_W x STAGE_H` (`1280 x 720`) stage, a press edge, and a
release edge.
{{else}}
The pointer belongs to the engine, which documents it in the `engine/` directory at the
root of this repository. What the game reads from it is a pointer position in the game's
logical units on the `STAGE_W x STAGE_H` (`1280 x 720`) stage, a press edge, and a
release edge, delivered as the ordered samples the player controller reads each frame.
{{/if}}

Every screen and every control is fully operable with the pointer alone. The keyboard
actions below are accelerators, with one exception: `modify` stands in for no control at
all and only modifies a pointer press, and the combine set it builds is a refinement of
a combine the game otherwise resolves on its own.

| Pointer act | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| Press on a control | Activates that control. A press at the center of a control's drawn rectangle activates it. |
| Press on the yard while holding a rock | Drops the rock, when the footprint is legal. A press on an illegal footprint places nothing and keeps the rock held. |
| Press on a structure | Selects it as the primary selection. |
| Press on empty yard | Clears the selection. |
| Press on a base structure while `modify` is held | Adds it to the explicit combine set, or removes it if it is already in the set. A press with `modify` released clears the set back to a single selection. |
| Move over the yard while holding a rock | Snaps the held footprint to the tile under the pointer and updates its legal read. |
| Move over the maze-length readout | Draws the full ground route on the yard. |
| Move over a leaderboard row | Spotlights that structure on the yard. |
| Move over a next-wave entry or a recipe entry | Floats that entry's tooltip. |

## Actions and bindings

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
`ACTIONS` holds the actions the game reads from the runtime layer, and `BINDINGS` maps
each to the key that fires it.
{{else}}
`ACTIONS` holds the actions the game registers with the engine, and `BINDINGS` maps each
to the key that fires it.
{{/if}}
Every action but `modify` is read as a press edge, so holding its key fires it once.
`modify` is read as a level instead: what the game reads is whether its key is down at
the moment it reads it, so it modifies whatever act it is held across.

| Action | Key | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `stamp` | `KeyB` | Pulls the press and arms a rock. |
| `keep` | `KeyK` | Harvests the selected candidate. |
| `downgrade` | `KeyG` | Harvests the selected candidate one quality tier lower. |
| `combine` | `KeyC` | Commits a combine from the current selection. |
| `upgrade` | `KeyU` | Raises the selected combination tower's level, or refines the press when the selection is not a combination tower. |
| `targeting` | `KeyT` | Cycles the selected firing structure's targeting priority. |
| `dismantle` | `KeyX` | Dismantles the selected structure. |
| `speed` | `KeyF` | Cycles the speed multiplier. |
| `pause` | `Space` | Toggles the in-place pause. |
| `combos` | `KeyV` | Toggles the recipe book. |
| `damage` | `KeyL` | Toggles the damage leaderboard. |
| `mute` | `KeyM` | Toggles audio mute. |
| `modify` | `ShiftLeft`, `ShiftRight` | Held rather than pressed. A press on the yard made while it is held adds to or removes from the explicit combine set. |
| `up` | `ArrowUp` | Moves the menu highlight up. |
| `down` | `ArrowDown` | Moves the menu highlight down. |
| `confirm` | `Enter` | Takes the highlighted menu entry. |
| `back` | `Escape` | Backs out, as the table below states. |

`back` resolves against the first of these that applies: a held rock is put away; the
selection is cleared; an open overlay is closed; on `playing` the pause menu opens; on
`paused` the pause menu closes; on any other screen the game returns to the previous
screen.

## When each action is available

| Action | Available |
| --- | --- |
| `stamp`, `keep`, `downgrade`, `dismantle` | During a build phase only. |
| `combine` | During a build phase, and during a wave when it folds standing structures only. |
| `upgrade`, `targeting` | In every phase, including during a wave and the finale. |
| `speed`, `pause`, `combos`, `damage`, `mute`, `modify` | On `playing`, in every phase. |
| `up`, `down`, `confirm` | On the menu screens. |
| `back` | Everywhere. |

A control that is unavailable is drawn disabled in its slot rather than removed, as
`specs/hud.md` states.

## The build controls

- Pulling the press arms a blank rock on the cursor. It is refused when the level's stamp
  allowance is spent, and the refusal reads clearly.
- Placing a rock spends one stamp and rolls its component where it lands. While stamps
  remain, another rock is armed immediately, so five are placed back to back.
- Keeping harvests the selected candidate. It is immediate and final: the candidate
  becomes a permanent component, every other candidate hardens into a blocker, and the
  wave starts.
- Downgrading harvests the selected candidate one quality tier lower, and starts the wave
  the same way. It is offered on a candidate at Tuned or above and disabled on a Scrap
  candidate.
- Combining resolves the instant it is committed. It is offered on a base structure when
  a matching partner or a reachable recipe exists. The inspector labels the quality fold
  `COMBINE` and each reachable recipe `COMBINE SPECIAL`, naming the tower it would build.
  It does not annotate whether a given fold starts the wave.
- Upgrading raises the selected combination tower one level, or, when the selection is
  not a combination tower, refines the press one level. Both are refused at their top
  rung and when unaffordable.
- Cycling targeting steps the selected firing structure's priority through `first`,
  `last`, `nearest`, `strongest`, `weakest`, and back to `first`, one step per activation.
- Dismantling removes the selected structure and reopens its tiles.

## Waves, speed, and pause

- There is no send control. A wave starts when the level's harvest is committed.
- The speed control cycles the multiplier through `1`, `2`, `4`, `8`, and back to `1`,
  one step per activation. It applies to the whole simulation and persists until changed.
- The in-place pause freezes the simulation without opening a menu. The yard stays
  visible and readable, and the status bar reads `PAUSED`. Activating it again resumes.
- The pause menu freezes the simulation and covers the yard, as `specs/ui.md` states.
  Resuming from it also clears any in-place pause.
